zstd — third-party attribution

This file carries a CONDITION. The encoder and the decoder in `src/` are a translation of C
source from libzstd (github.com/facebook/zstd, tag v1.5.7, commit
f8745da6ff1ad1e7bab384bd1f9d742439278e99) into Zig. The BSD licence that source
is offered under requires its copyright notice, conditions and disclaimer to
travel with redistributions of the source and to be reproduced with binary
redistributions. They are reproduced in full below. The obligation lives here,
beside the code that owes it; the root NOTICE does not list modules.

**Copyleft:** NONE-SHIPPED — libzstd is dual-licensed "BSD-style OR GPLv2" at
the recipient's option. This port is taken under the BSD licence only; no text
of this module is offered under, or relies on, the GPLv2.

WHAT WAS TAKEN

Translated (source, restructured into Zig but decision-for-decision the same):

  lib/compress/zstd_fast.c            no-dictionary and extDict `fast`
                                      match finders                         -> src/match.zig
  lib/compress/zstd_double_fast.c     no-dictionary and extDict `dfast`
                                      match finders                         -> src/match.zig
  lib/compress/zstd_lazy.c            no-dictionary and extDict hash-chain,
                                      row and binary-tree (DUBT) match
                                      finders, greedy/lazy/lazy2/btlazy2
                                      parsers                               -> src/lazy.zig
  lib/compress/zstd_opt.c             no-dictionary binary-tree match
                                      finder, price model and optimal
                                      parser (btopt/btultra/btultra2), with
                                      its long-distance candidates, and
                                      their extDict variants                -> src/opt.zig
  lib/compress/zstd_ldm.c,            long-distance matching: gear rolling
  lib/compress/zstd_ldm_geartab.h     hash and its table, bucketed match
                                      table, sequence generation (prefix
                                      and extDict)                          -> src/ldm.zig
  lib/compress/zstd_compress_internal.h  window helpers, hashes, ZSTD_count,
                                      seqStore, repcode handling            -> src/match.zig, src/sequences.zig
  lib/compress/zstd_compress.c        frame/block driver (compressContinue,
                                      compressEnd), frame header, parameter
                                      adjustment, entropy glue for a block  -> src/frame.zig, src/params.zig
                                      dictionary loading (insertDictionary,
                                      loadCEntropy, loadDictionaryContent)
                                      and the CDict                         -> src/cdict.zig
                                      a CDict into a context (copy, reload,
                                      attach), prefixes, usingDict/CDict    -> src/frame.zig
                                      streaming (compressStream2 over
                                      buffered input and output)            -> src/stream.zig
                                      post-block splitter and its block
                                      size estimates                        -> src/blocksplit.zig
  lib/compress/zstd_compress_superblock.c  superblocks (targetCBlockSize)   -> src/superblock.zig
  lib/compress/clevels.h              level tables                          -> src/params.zig
  lib/compress/zstd_preSplit.c        block pre-splitter                    -> src/presplit.zig
  lib/compress/zstd_compress_literals.c  literals section                  -> src/literals.zig
  lib/compress/zstd_compress_sequences.c encoding-type choice, table build,
                                      sequence bitstream                    -> src/sequences.zig
  lib/compress/huf_compress.c         Huffman tree, table header (writing
                                      and, for dictionaries, reading),
                                      streams                               -> src/huf.zig
  lib/compress/fse_compress.c, lib/common/fse.h
                                      FSE normalisation, header, coding     -> src/fse.zig
  lib/common/bitstream.h              bit writer                            -> src/bitstream.zig
  lib/compress/hist.c                 byte histograms                       -> src/hist.zig
  lib/common/zstd_internal.h          code tables, default distributions    -> src/sequences.zig
  lib/decompress/zstd_decompress.c    frame decoder (one-shot and
                                      piecewise), frame header, size
                                      queries, skippable frames,
                                      loadDEntropy, getDictID_from*         -> src/decompress.zig, src/ddict.zig
                                      streaming (decompressStream)          -> src/dstream.zig
  lib/decompress/zstd_ddict.c         DDict: load, copy/ref, dictID        -> src/ddict.zig
  lib/decompress/zstd_decompress_block.c, lib/decompress/zstd_decompress_internal.h
                                      literals and sequences sections,
                                      sequence tables, sequence execution   -> src/dblock.zig
  lib/decompress/huf_decompress.c     Huffman decoding tables and streams,
                                      incl. the fast four-stream loop       -> src/huf_dec.zig
  lib/common/entropy_common.c         FSE_readNCount, HUF_readStats         -> src/dbits.zig, src/huf_dec.zig
  lib/common/fse_decompress.c, lib/common/bitstream.h
                                      FSE decoding, bit reader              -> src/dbits.zig
  lib/dictBuilder/cover.c, lib/dictBuilder/cover.h, lib/dictBuilder/fastcover.c
                                      dictionary training up to
                                      finalization: cover and fastCover
                                      contexts, segment selection, epochs,
                                      parameter checks, the optimizers'
                                      parameter grid                        -> src/dict_builder.zig

Each of those files says so in its first line
(`SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause AND MIT`). `src/root.zig`, the tests
and `src/testdata/` are this collection's own work (MIT).

Not taken: the dictMatchState (attached dictionary) variants of the `fast`
and `dfast` match finders (the others are ported), training a dictionary
past content selection (`zdict.c`'s finalization step), the prefetching
sequence decoder, the x86-64 assembly Huffman loop (its C twin is ported),
long-distance matching below `btopt`, multithreading, `targetCBlockSize`
super-blocks.

Run, not copied: `tools/` builds the same libzstd tag and runs it to produce
`src/testdata/goldens.zig` and `src/testdata/stream_goldens.zig` (lengths and
SHA-256 digests of its output). `tools/zref.c`, `tools/zstream.c` and
`tools/zdec.c` (the decoder's differential oracle) and `tools/zdtrain.c`
are this collection's own programs (MIT) calling libzstd's public API;
`tools/ztrain.c` (MIT) `#include`s libzstd's `cover.c` / `fastcover.c` at
build time to call their internal steps, and writes
`src/testdata/dict_goldens.zig` through `tools/gen-dict-goldens.sh`. No
libzstd source bytes are stored in this repository; the two trained
dictionaries `src/testdata/*.zdict` are libzstd's output (its trainer,
`ZDICT_trainFromBuffer`, run on this collection's generated samples), as
the golden digests are.

